// The validation corpus of the zenoh verdict (docs/flow-zenoh-verdict.md §6.12).
//
// Collected after model 6 was frozen (ledger round 4158), of what the
// development corpus (captures/corpus/) lacks, and counted into no weight until
// the one reading section 6.13 reports. The format is captures/corpus/'s:
// every file is a REAL capture, anonymised by scripts/lib/capture_anonymise.py
// (scope "own": traffic this capture made itself), and
// `capture_anonymise.py --verify-corpus captures/validation` holds every file to
// being one the anonymiser would leave as it is.
//
// How each was taken is scripts/capture-validation.sh: a zenoh workload on a
// container's loopback with zenohd and the examples of the pinned release
// (1.10.2), zenoh-c 1.10.2 or zenoh-pico 1.10.2; a null protocol's real server
// and client in containers on a docker network of their own, captured in the
// server's network namespace. Every file is a group of its own: a workload, a
// link, an implementation or a null protocol (section 6.3).
{
  groups: [
